flowchart TB
  accTitle: How a new discussion gets its first answer
  accDescr: A new discussion starts discussion-assistant.yml. Its event job runs no AI and lets a discussion through only when its category is one of answer_categories, someone who doesn't maintain the repository opened it, and the day has room in max_per_day and max_per_author_per_day, which count new issues and discussions together. Then analyze lets the AI read the discussion, the issues and the other discussions with tools that only read, and answer with JSON. The apply job reads the discussion again and posts nothing when it is closed or locked, has an answer, or a maintainer commented first, or when the answer fails a check. Otherwise it posts one comment, which it never marks as the answer; a bug or a feature request also gets a link to the forms of the issues.
  opened(["a new discussion"]) --> event{"`**event**: a category of<br>answer_categories, not a<br>maintainer, room in the limits?`"}
  event -- "no" --> none["no answer;<br>the run notes why"]
  event -- "yes" --> analyze["`**analyze**<br>the AI reads the discussion,<br>the issues and the other<br>discussions, answers with JSON`"]
  analyze --> apply{"`**apply**: still open, no answer,<br>no maintainer yet, and every<br>check of the answer passes?`"}
  apply -- "no" --> none
  apply -- "yes" --> posted["one comment, never marked<br>as the answer; a bug or a<br>feature request links the<br>forms of the issues"]
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef ai fill:#8250df33,stroke:#8250df,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef person fill:#0969da26,stroke:#0969da,stroke-width:2px
  class opened trigger
  class event,apply question
  class analyze ai
  class posted job
  class none person
